contentText:
Dolly Parton &#8216;s sister Stella Parton has shared a message in the wake of the country superstar&#8217;s death, asking people online to &#8220;show more compassion&#8221; as her family navigates the loss.

On Friday (Sept. 4), Stella posted a two-slide letter to Instagram marking 10 days since Dolly died at the age of 80 following a brief cancer battle. &#8220;We will be okay in time but each of us will grieve in our own personal way,&#8221; Stella wrote in the message. &#8220;Sadly, because of the way our lives have been in front of the public, we have no choice but to be subjected to incredible pressure and insensitivity from strangers.&#8221;

